# Written by pm-flow's installer into the flow directory itself, so a repository
# that installs pm-flow needs no edits of its own to stay clean.
#
# The rule is the same one the store is built on: definitions are committed,
# records are not. Everything below is something the flow writes while working.

# The store. One file per project, rewritten on every dispatch. Committing it
# recreates exactly the churn it exists to remove.
*/runs/pm_flow.db
*/runs/pm_flow.db-wal
*/runs/pm_flow.db-shm

# Per-dispatch run records: transcripts, prompts, response envelopes, the cost
# ledger. The store holds the same facts in a form you can query.
*/runs/*
!*/runs/.gitkeep

# Cycle working files. A section's brief, state and handoff are worth keeping;
# the scratch of each attempt is not.
*/sections/*/cycles/
*/sections/*/panels/
*/sections/*/escalation*/

# Locks and claims. Runtime coordination, meaningless once the process is gone.
*.lock
.claim-*

# The repo-local environment hook. It exists to hold things like API base URLs
# and tokens, so it must never be committed. `local_env.sh.example` is tracked.
local_env.sh

__pycache__/
*.pyc
